It is Wednesday afternoon.
It is very cold in the office because of the AC.
Rohan and I come outside for a short break.
We go to a tea vendor on the street.
I say, "Brother, please give two cutting chais."
The tea vendor gives us hot tea in small glasses.
The fresh outside air feels very good.
Rohan asks me, "Maya, how have you liked the new project?"
I reply, "I have liked it a lot."
"We have all worked a lot this week."
Rohan smiles and drinks his tea.
He says, "Yes, Suresh has chosen a good project."
We talk about life in Mumbai.
I say, "I have learned a lot here."
"Now I have gotten used to Mumbai's hustle and bustle and cutting chai."
Rohan laughs.
He says, "You have started speaking exactly like a Mumbaikar!"
We finish our tea and go back to the office.
